,"type":"saver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1824","fullName":"TD Garden","address":{"city":"Boston","state":"MA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1824.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17850,"officials":[{"fullName":"Alex Lepkowski","displayName":"Alex Lepkowski","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"TJ Luxmore","displayName":"TJ Luxmore","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Joe Mahon","displayName":"Joe Mahon","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jeremy Faucher","displayName":"Jeremy Faucher","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Fraser Minten has a goal and two assists as Bruins roll past winless Flyers 5-1","description":"— Fraser Minten had a goal and two assists, Pavel Zacha scored his first goal of the season and the Boston Bruins beat the struggling Philadelphia Flyers 5-1 on Saturday.","story":"BOSTON -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080207/fraser-minten\">Fraser Minten</a> had a goal and two assists, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899949/pavel-zacha\">Pavel Zacha</a> scored his first goal of the season and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/bos/boston-bruins\">Boston Bruins</a> beat the struggling <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> 5-1 on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697461/mason-lohrei\">Mason Lohrei</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697442/marat-khusnutdinov\">Marat Khusnutdinov</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233575/casey-mittelstadt\">Casey Mittelstadt</a> also scored for Boston (4-2), which won its second straight game.\n\n\r\n              Starting for the fifth time in the Bruins’ first six games, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4712036/jeremy-swayman\">Jeremy Swayman</a> faced just three shots in the opening 30 minutes and finished with 14 saves. His bid for his second shutout of the season was spoiled when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291941/porter-martone\">Porter Martone</a> had a power-play goal 6:32 into the final period. Swayman won his 136th game, tying Andy Moog for eighth on Boston's all-time list.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942459/dan-vladar\">Dan Vladar</a> made 27 saves for the Flyers (0-4-2), who are the Eastern Conference’s only winless team.\n\n\r\n              Top Boston defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3988803/charlie-mcavoy\">Charlie McAvoy</a> served the final of his <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/bruins-mcavoy-suspension-c2d6715b6cb7ef485c1420e5bda0b8f4\">six-game suspension</a> to start the season from a slashing incident during last spring’s playoffs.\n\n\r\n              Coming off a lopsided win over Utah at home on Thursday, the Bruins jumped ahead on Zacha’s goal 12:21 into the opening period when he took a backhand pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114778/david-pastrnak\">David Pastrnak</a> in the slot and fired a wrister that broke into the net off Vladar’s right pad.\n\n\r\n              Following a tough loss at Ottawa on Thursday, the Flyers were outshot 19-3 in the opening 30 minutes and 22-8 after two periods.\n\n\r\n              Lohrei beat Vladar over his shoulder with a wrister with 2:48 left in the second, making it 2-0.\n\n\r\n              Khusnutdinov scored off a nice feed from Minten just under two minutes into the third.\n\n\r\n              Flyers winger Michael Bunting played his second game after <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/flyers-sign-michael-bunting-8e16cf5072baa40d662404d9900ab608\">signing as a free agent this week.</a>\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Flyers: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/car/carolina-hurricanes\">Carolina Hurricanes</a> on Sunday night.\n\n\r\n              Bruins: Visit the San Jose Shark on Tuesday night, the first of a four-game road trip.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-10T19:46:27Z"}}